{
  "kanji": "押",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 押\ntitle: push\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 8\nradical: 手\nradicalNumber: 64\nonyomi: [オウ]\nkunyomi: [お.す, お.し-, お.っ-, お.さえる, おさ.える]\ndistractors: [田, 指, 招]\n---\n\n# 押 — push\n\n**Strokes:** 8 · **Key (radical):** 手 (as 扌, no. 64) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n押 concerns pushing or applying pressure. [押す](../words/押す.md) おす is the verb to learn for pushing a door.\n押さえる おさえる can mean holding something down or steady, so pressure need not produce movement.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** picture 扌 pressing against the box-shaped part of 甲 on the right.\nThe vertical line continues below the box. This is a visual memory aid, not etymology.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe source preserves two dot divisions for おさえる; they represent the same spoken word here.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| お.す | kun | [押す](../words/押す.md) おす — push |\n| お.さえる | kun | 押さえる おさえる — hold down; keep steady |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [押す](../words/押す.md) おす — push\n- 押さえる おさえる — hold down; hold in place\n\n## Notes\n\nドアを押す means \"push the door.\" The contrasting action is [引く](../words/引く.md) ひく, \"pull.\"\nThat is a contrast of actions, not a claim that the two verbs oppose each other in every expression.\n\nThe right side of 押 is not simply [田](田.md): its central line extends below.\n[指](指.md) and [招](招.md) share 扌 but arrange the right-hand strokes differently.\n\nSources: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project);\n[JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1180470, 1589080, 1169250.\n",
